Drop the drmP.h include from the drm_fb_helper_fill_info autoconf probe.

drmP.h was removed from mainline kernels before v7.3.  The out-of-tree kcl
header at include/kcl/header/drm/drmP.h is a no-op wrapper when
HAVE_DRM_DRMP_H is unset.  Because the autoconf compile-test includes
drmP.h from the *kernel* headers directory (not the kcl shadow path), the
test fails on any kernel that no longer ships drmP.h, and the flag
HAVE_DRM_FB_HELPER_FILL_INFO is never defined.

When the flag is absent, kcl_drm_fb.c attempts to implement
drm_fb_helper_fill_info() by calling drm_fb_helper_fill_fix() and
drm_fb_helper_fill_var(), both of which became file-scope static helpers
inside drm_fb_helper.c in v7.x and are therefore unreachable from
out-of-tree code.

Fix: remove the superfluous drmP.h include from the AC_KERNEL_TRY_COMPILE
body.  drm_fb_helper.h is self-contained; the function prototype for
drm_fb_helper_fill_info() is declared there directly.

--- a/amd/dkms/m4/drm-fb-helper-fill-info.m4
+++ b/amd/dkms/m4/drm-fb-helper-fill-info.m4
@@ -5,7 +5,6 @@
 AC_DEFUN([AC_AMDGPU_DRM_FB_HELPER_FILL_INFO], [
 	AC_KERNEL_DO_BACKGROUND([
 		AC_KERNEL_TRY_COMPILE([
-			#include <drm/drmP.h>
 			#include <drm/drm_fb_helper.h>
 		], [
 			drm_fb_helper_fill_info(NULL, NULL, NULL);
